WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:03.701
-The select House committee
investigating

00:00:03.701 --> 00:00:05.534
Donald Trump's attempted coup
on January 6th

00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:06.968
held its second hearing today,

00:00:06.968 --> 00:00:09.601
and it was just as damning
as the first, with multiple

00:00:09.601 --> 00:00:13.267
Trump aides and advisers
on tape confirming

00:00:13.267 --> 00:00:16.133
that there was no evidence
for Trump's stolen election lies

00:00:16.133 --> 00:00:18.200
and that they had told
Trump repeatedly

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:20.133
that there was no evidence
for those lies.

00:00:20.133 --> 00:00:23.100
Oh, also, Rudy Giuliani
was wasted on election night.

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:25.801
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:25.801 --> 00:00:27.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:30.167 --> 00:00:33.234
Today's hearing was no less a
blockbuster than the first one,

00:00:33.234 --> 00:00:35.667
which is saying a lot, given
how many bombshells there were

00:00:35.667 --> 00:00:37.000
in the first hearing last week.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:40.400
Today, the committee laid out
in painstaking detail

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:43.234
the degree to which virtually
everyone around Trump,

00:00:43.234 --> 00:00:45.567
from his campaign manager
to his attorney general

00:00:45.567 --> 00:00:47.033
to his own family,

00:00:47.033 --> 00:00:50.067
knew that there was
no evidence of election fraud

00:00:50.067 --> 00:00:53.434
and told Trump there was
no evidence of fraud.

00:00:53.434 --> 00:00:56.534
-They wasted a whole month
on these claims

00:00:56.534 --> 00:01:00.767
on the Dominion voting machines,
and they were idiotic claims.

00:01:00.767 --> 00:01:05.334
I told them that it was --
it was crazy stuff

00:01:05.334 --> 00:01:07.167
and they were wasting their time
on that.

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:11.601
All the early claims
that I understood

00:01:11.601 --> 00:01:14.100
were completely bogus and silly,

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:17.000
and usually based on
complete misinformation.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:18.334
-Told him flat out

00:01:18.334 --> 00:01:21.334
that much of the information
he's getting is false

00:01:21.334 --> 00:01:24.534
and/or just not supported
by the evidence.

00:01:24.534 --> 00:01:27.200
We look at the allegations,
but they don't pan out.

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:30.300
-So, this wild claim
is thrown out,

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:33.300
which, you know,
on its face didn't seem,

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:35.334
you know, realistic
or possible to me.

00:01:35.334 --> 00:01:38.567
-I thought
the Dominion stuff was...

00:01:38.567 --> 00:01:40.400
I never saw any evidence
whatsoever

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:41.901
to sustain those allegations.

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:46.267
What they were proposing,
I thought was nuts.

00:01:46.267 --> 00:01:49.634
The theory was also
completely nuts, right?

00:01:49.634 --> 00:01:52.234
I mean, it was a combination
of the Italians, the Germans.

00:01:52.234 --> 00:01:54.734
I mean, different things
had been floating around

00:01:54.734 --> 00:01:56.067
as to who was involved,

00:01:56.067 --> 00:01:57.834
Hugo Chávez
and the Venezuelans.

00:01:57.834 --> 00:02:00.534
-I told him that the stuff that
his people were shoveling out

00:02:00.534 --> 00:02:02.868
to the public were --
was bullshit.

00:02:02.868 --> 00:02:05.467
I mean that the claims of fraud
were bullshit.

00:02:05.467 --> 00:02:06.968
-Of course it was
all bull[bleep].

00:02:06.968 --> 00:02:08.934
It's like Trump asked
for a story

00:02:08.934 --> 00:02:11.334
that explained why he lost
and his team said,

00:02:11.334 --> 00:02:13.200
"How much time do we have
to come up with it?"

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:15.033
And he said, "Three seconds!"
And they said,

00:02:15.033 --> 00:02:17.767
"Uh, uh, a dead
Venezuelan dictator

00:02:17.767 --> 00:02:20.167
teamed with, um,
an election software company

00:02:20.167 --> 00:02:22.267
and the governments of Italy,
Germany, and China

00:02:22.267 --> 00:02:23.734
to stuff fraudulent ballots

00:02:23.734 --> 00:02:25.367
into suitcases
and shopping carts?"

00:02:25.367 --> 00:02:29.234
[As Trump] Oh, that's good.
You guys are worth every penny.

00:02:29.234 --> 00:02:31.567
[Normal voice] Actually -- uh,
actually, sir, you don't pay us.

00:02:31.567 --> 00:02:33.400
[As Trump] Exactly.

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:36.567
[Normal voice] Everyone around
Trump knew it was bull[bleep]

00:02:36.567 --> 00:02:38.601
and told Trump
it was bull[bleep]

00:02:38.601 --> 00:02:39.868
over and over
and over again.

00:02:39.868 --> 00:02:41.901
But Trump went ahead and
declared the election stolen

00:02:41.901 --> 00:02:44.667
anyway and spent months
spreading that lie,

00:02:44.667 --> 00:02:46.634
despite hearing repeatedly
from his closest aides

00:02:46.634 --> 00:02:48.334
and advisers that what
he was saying was insane.

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:51.734
And documenting that Trump knew
it was all bull[bleep]

00:02:51.734 --> 00:02:53.501
is important for establishing
his frame of mind.

00:02:53.501 --> 00:02:54.868
He obviously had
criminal intent.

00:02:54.868 --> 00:02:57.567
I know this is obvious,
but still, it's important

00:02:57.567 --> 00:03:00.300
to establish that he wasn't
just, like, innocently

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:02.334
investigating credible
allegations of fraud.

00:03:02.334 --> 00:03:04.868
He was actively trying
to overturn an election

00:03:04.868 --> 00:03:06.968
he knew he did not win,
and engaged

00:03:06.968 --> 00:03:08.767
in many potentially
criminal activities to do it,

00:03:08.767 --> 00:03:11.300
including fomenting
a violent attack on the Capitol.

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:13.334
In fact, Trump's campaign
manager, Bill Stepien,

00:03:13.334 --> 00:03:15.000
even said in one deposition

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:18.834
that he and other Trump aides
who knew there wasn't fraud

00:03:18.834 --> 00:03:21.968
had been divided into a separate
group from all the crazy people,

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:25.968
and the non-crazy people
even had an informal name.

00:03:25.968 --> 00:03:28.100
-I didn't mind being
categorized.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:30.100
There were two groups of them.

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:32.801
We called them kind of my team
and Rudy's team.

00:03:32.801 --> 00:03:34.601
I didn't mind
being characterized

00:03:34.601 --> 00:03:36.467
as being part of Team Normal,

00:03:36.467 --> 00:03:40.434
as reporters kind of started
to do around that point in time.

00:03:40.434 --> 00:03:42.634
-That's right, they were known
as Team Normal.

00:03:42.634 --> 00:03:46.234
Now, I could tell you
the specific names of the people

00:03:46.234 --> 00:03:48.300
who were supposedly
on Team Normal.

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:51.868
Or I could just tell you that
none of them look like this.

00:03:51.868 --> 00:03:53.701
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:53.701 --> 00:03:57.167
[As Giuliani] Hey, I'm here
for Team Normal tryouts.

00:03:57.167 --> 00:03:59.501
[Normal voice] Actually,
I'm sorry, Team Normal's full.

00:03:59.501 --> 00:04:01.767
[As Giuliani] Be honest.
Was it my eyes?

00:04:01.767 --> 00:04:04.267
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:04.267 --> 00:04:06.934
[Normal voice] Also -- Also,
in regards to Stepien,

00:04:06.934 --> 00:04:08.601
I'd argue
that despite his resistance

00:04:08.601 --> 00:04:09.934
to Trump's fraud claims,

00:04:09.934 --> 00:04:11.734
he was still just as complicit
as anyone else,

00:04:11.734 --> 00:04:13.501
given that he was managing
Trump's campaign

00:04:13.501 --> 00:04:15.667
even while Trump
was preemptively claiming

00:04:15.667 --> 00:04:17.701
the election would be rigged,
and never once spoke out

00:04:17.701 --> 00:04:19.434
to warn the public
about how dangerous Trump was.

00:04:19.434 --> 00:04:22.300
And yet, for some reason, the
photo they used of him all day

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:24.334
made him look kick-ass.

00:04:24.334 --> 00:04:26.667
Look at my man
So-Called Life-in' it

00:04:26.667 --> 00:04:29.167
Claire Danes style.

00:04:29.167 --> 00:04:31.334
God, it' so cool that
she grew up to be in the CIA.

00:04:31.334 --> 00:04:33.033
And whatever happened
to that other guy?

00:04:33.033 --> 00:04:34.601
Aah!

00:04:34.601 --> 00:04:37.434
Fun fact -- they put him
on Team Normal before Rudy.

00:04:37.434 --> 00:04:39.300
Either way, Trump obviously

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:41.000
decided to go with Rudy
over Team Normal.

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:42.400
Now, early in her
opening statement,

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:43.868
Congresswoman Liz Cheney

00:04:43.868 --> 00:04:47.033
teased that the hearing
would touch upon Rudy's role

00:04:47.033 --> 00:04:49.267
in the attempted coup
when she said this.

00:04:49.267 --> 00:04:51.801
-You will also hear testimony
that President Trump

00:04:51.801 --> 00:04:54.234
rejected the advice
of his campaign experts

00:04:54.234 --> 00:04:55.801
on election night

00:04:55.801 --> 00:04:58.868
and instead followed
the course recommended

00:04:58.868 --> 00:05:02.133
by an apparently inebriated
Rudy Giuliani

00:05:02.133 --> 00:05:07.334
to just claim he won and insist
that the vote counting stop,

00:05:07.334 --> 00:05:10.200
to falsely claim
everything was fraudulent.

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:12.033
-I mean, that is brutal.
It's embarrassing to have

00:05:12.033 --> 00:05:13.734
a member of Congress announce

00:05:13.734 --> 00:05:15.834
on live television
that you were visibly drunk.

00:05:15.834 --> 00:05:19.067
I mean, I've been visibly drunk
on TV before,

00:05:19.067 --> 00:05:22.067
but it's for entertainment.

00:05:22.067 --> 00:05:24.467
Never once during any of
my Day Drinking episodes

00:05:24.467 --> 00:05:27.968
have I ever said to my guest,
"Hey, you wanna do a coup?"

00:05:27.968 --> 00:05:29.000
[ Laughter ]

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:30.667
And let me make something
perfectly clear.

00:05:30.667 --> 00:05:32.167
If Rihanna had suggested it,

00:05:32.167 --> 00:05:34.667
I would have been down
at the Capitol in a heartbeat.

00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:36.000
[ Laughter ]

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:37.634
Now, when Cheney said
Rudy was inebriated,

00:05:37.634 --> 00:05:38.968
I thought, "Damn,
that's embarrassing,

00:05:38.968 --> 00:05:40.767
But I guess
that's the end of that."

00:05:40.767 --> 00:05:43.200
What I could have never
imagined in my wildest dreams

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:46.100
was that it was just a tease
for what was coming up,

00:05:46.100 --> 00:05:48.200
because it turns out
a significant portion

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:50.133
of the hearing,
bolstered by witness testimony,

00:05:50.133 --> 00:05:52.534
focused on
former Mayor Giuliani,

00:05:52.534 --> 00:05:55.300
an attorney to the president
of the United States,

00:05:55.300 --> 00:05:57.901
being blitzed
out of his [bleep] mind.

00:05:57.901 --> 00:05:59.567
-Were you in
the White House residence

00:05:59.567 --> 00:06:01.901
during the sort of --
past midnight

00:06:01.901 --> 00:06:04.901
into the early morning hours
of November 4th?

00:06:07.267 --> 00:06:09.300
-Yes. Oh, sure.
It went over beyond midnight.

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:12.033
Yes.
-Do you remember Rudy Giuliani

00:06:12.033 --> 00:06:14.334
being at the White House
on election night

00:06:14.334 --> 00:06:16.968
and into the early hours
the next morning?

00:06:16.968 --> 00:06:18.634
-I do.

00:06:18.634 --> 00:06:20.634
-What do you remember
about when he came?

00:06:22.534 --> 00:06:24.868
-Um...
[ Clears throat ]

00:06:24.868 --> 00:06:26.334
He...

00:06:28.067 --> 00:06:29.567
He was, um...

00:06:29.567 --> 00:06:30.667
They were...

00:06:30.667 --> 00:06:33.734
I had heard that
he was upstairs, you know,

00:06:33.734 --> 00:06:37.000
in that aforementioned
reception area.

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:40.467
And, um...

00:06:40.467 --> 00:06:43.133
he was looking
to talk to the president.

00:06:43.133 --> 00:06:47.200
And it was suggested
instead that he come talk

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:51.534
to several of us
down off the Map Room.

00:06:51.534 --> 00:06:54.000
-Was there anyone
in that conversation

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:57.767
who, in your observation,
had had too much to drink?

00:07:00.067 --> 00:07:03.067
-Um, like Mayor Giuliani.

00:07:03.067 --> 00:07:04.934
-Tell me more about that.
What was your observation

00:07:04.934 --> 00:07:10.300
about his potential intoxication
during that -- that discussion

00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:13.567
about what the president
should say

00:07:13.567 --> 00:07:17.067
when he addressed the nation
on election night?

00:07:17.067 --> 00:07:21.734
-The mayor was definitely
intoxicated, but I do not know

00:07:21.734 --> 00:07:23.701
his level of intoxication

00:07:23.701 --> 00:07:26.534
when he spoke
with the president, for example.

00:07:26.534 --> 00:07:28.767
-It's so funny to me
how in all these deposition,

00:07:28.767 --> 00:07:30.467
Trump aides are all
hemming and hawing,

00:07:30.467 --> 00:07:32.701
pausing and taking their time
to use the most precise

00:07:32.701 --> 00:07:34.801
legal language possible
because they're under oath.

00:07:34.801 --> 00:07:36.267
But then, as soon
as someone asks,

00:07:36.267 --> 00:07:37.734
"Was anyone drunk
at the White House?"

00:07:37.734 --> 00:07:40.133
they all immediately buzz in
like the overeager uncle

00:07:40.133 --> 00:07:41.334
on "Family Feud."

00:07:41.334 --> 00:07:42.734
"Rudy! It was Rudy!"

00:07:42.734 --> 00:07:43.968
[ Laughter ]

00:07:43.968 --> 00:07:45.701
In fact, if "Who was drunk
at the White House?"

00:07:45.701 --> 00:07:47.200
was a question on "Family Feud,"

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:49.701
the top five answers
would all be the same.

00:07:49.701 --> 00:07:51.000
[ Laughter ]

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:53.167
Also, I love the follow-up
where the lawyer says,

00:07:53.167 --> 00:07:54.534
"Tell me more about that."

00:07:54.534 --> 00:07:56.868
I wish I could have seen
the rest of that deposition.

00:07:56.868 --> 00:07:59.300
"And how did you know
Rudy was drunk?"

00:07:59.300 --> 00:08:02.067
"Well, I saw him holding
an empty bottle of Scotch

00:08:02.067 --> 00:08:04.434
and hitting on a portrait
of Dolley Madison."

00:08:04.434 --> 00:08:06.000
[As Giuliani]
Well, hello, young lady!

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:07.667
Now, before we go any further,

00:08:07.667 --> 00:08:09.534
you have a legal obligation
to tell me

00:08:09.534 --> 00:08:11.200
if you're my cousin.

00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:13.200
[ Laughter ]

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:15.300
Fool me twice!

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:17.634
[ Laughter ]

00:08:17.634 --> 00:08:19.567
[Normal voice] So,
as the committee established,

00:08:19.567 --> 00:08:22.367
Trump had a choice between
Team Normal and Team Rudy,

00:08:22.367 --> 00:08:24.133
and obviously
he chose Team Rudy.

00:08:24.133 --> 00:08:26.033
In fact, Trump's son-in-law,
Jared Kushner,

00:08:26.033 --> 00:08:28.601
who looked in every clip
like he had just smelled

00:08:28.601 --> 00:08:30.033
one of Rudy's Scotch farts,

00:08:30.033 --> 00:08:33.868
said at one point that he tried
to warn Trump about Rudy,

00:08:33.868 --> 00:08:35.667
although you could tell Kushner
was definitely walking

00:08:35.667 --> 00:08:37.300
on eggshells
when he answered the question.

00:08:37.300 --> 00:08:39.267
-Did you ever share,
Mr. Kushner,

00:08:39.267 --> 00:08:40.934
your view of Mr. Giuliani?

00:08:40.934 --> 00:08:42.634
Did you ever share
your perspective about him

00:08:42.634 --> 00:08:43.968
with the president?

00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:47.801
-Um...

00:08:47.801 --> 00:08:49.467
I-I guess...

00:08:51.033 --> 00:08:52.701
[ Sighs ]

00:08:52.701 --> 00:08:54.901
Uh...yes.

00:08:54.901 --> 00:08:56.167
[ Laughter ]

00:08:56.167 --> 00:08:57.601
-Tell me what you said.

00:08:57.601 --> 00:09:00.267
-Basically, "Not the approach
I would take if I was you."

00:09:00.267 --> 00:09:01.767
-Okay. And how did he react?

00:09:01.767 --> 00:09:03.067
How did President Trump react

00:09:03.067 --> 00:09:05.701
when you shared
that view with him?

00:09:05.701 --> 00:09:09.767
-Oh, he said, you know,
"I have confidence in Rudy."

00:09:09.767 --> 00:09:11.601
-That was a very long pause.

00:09:11.601 --> 00:09:14.501
You could tell Kushner did not
want to answer the question.

00:09:14.501 --> 00:09:16.367
I'm shocked he didn't break out
into a song called

00:09:16.367 --> 00:09:18.567
"We Don't Talk About Rudy."

00:09:18.567 --> 00:09:20.968
That's definitely the length
of the pause you take

00:09:20.968 --> 00:09:22.501
when someone asks you
about a friend

00:09:22.501 --> 00:09:23.934
who was super drunk at a party,

00:09:23.934 --> 00:09:25.934
especially a friend
you invited.

00:09:25.934 --> 00:09:28.067
"Hey, uh, you know
your friend Kyle?"

00:09:28.067 --> 00:09:29.400
"Uh..."

00:09:30.400 --> 00:09:32.067
[ Laughter ]

00:09:32.067 --> 00:09:34.701
[ Sighs ]

00:09:34.701 --> 00:09:36.868
"Yeeeeah."

00:09:36.868 --> 00:09:38.400
"He just did a cannonball
in the pool

00:09:38.400 --> 00:09:39.868
with all his clothes on
and told everyone

00:09:39.868 --> 00:09:41.200
if they didn't do
a Jell-O shot with him,

00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:42.367
he'd have them arrested."

00:09:42.367 --> 00:09:43.367
"Yeah, but so what?"

00:09:43.367 --> 00:09:46.133
"Well, it's a kid's
birthday party."

00:09:46.133 --> 00:09:48.133
So, today's hearing
was laser-focused

00:09:48.133 --> 00:09:49.467
on disproving the big lie

00:09:49.467 --> 00:09:51.300
and showing the public
that everyone around Trump,

00:09:51.300 --> 00:09:53.000
except for the drunk
and/or crazy people,

00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:54.667
thought the fraud claims
were insane

00:09:54.667 --> 00:09:57.434
and told Trump
those claims were insane.

00:09:57.434 --> 00:09:58.734
And here's a key point.

00:09:58.734 --> 00:10:00.400
A lot of people
are watching these hearings.

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:02.000
So proving that Trump
was both full of [bleep]

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:03.467
and knew he was full of [bleep]
is important

00:10:03.467 --> 00:10:06.634
because a big question going
into these hearings last week

00:10:06.634 --> 00:10:08.033
was whether people
would watch.

00:10:08.033 --> 00:10:10.834
Republicans and right-wing media
personalities, for example,

00:10:10.834 --> 00:10:14.501
were invested heavily in
the idea that no one would watch

00:10:14.501 --> 00:10:16.501
because they had better things
to do, but they were wrong.

00:10:16.501 --> 00:10:18.634
And audience of at least
20 million people

00:10:18.634 --> 00:10:20.234
watched the first
prime-time hearing,

00:10:20.234 --> 00:10:21.634
in the ballpark
of television events

00:10:21.634 --> 00:10:23.300
like a big
"Sunday Night Football" game

00:10:23.300 --> 00:10:25.133
or the Macy's
Thanksgiving Day Parade.

00:10:25.133 --> 00:10:26.767
And I'm not surprised
the hearing

00:10:26.767 --> 00:10:28.300
got Thanksgiving Parade ratings

00:10:28.300 --> 00:10:29.968
since so many
of Trump's inner circle

00:10:29.968 --> 00:10:31.901
look like they could be
balloons.

00:10:31.901 --> 00:10:33.133
[ Laughter ]

00:10:33.133 --> 00:10:35.467
"Oh, look, kid,
it's the Mike Lindell balloon!

00:10:35.467 --> 00:10:37.601
Oh, stop crying. It's not him.
It's just a balloon.

00:10:37.601 --> 00:10:38.934
Oh, wait. Okay.

00:10:38.934 --> 00:10:41.033
I actually do think
it actually might be him."

00:10:41.033 --> 00:10:42.367
[As Lindell]
"Yeah, it's me, alright!

00:10:42.367 --> 00:10:44.534
They just tied some strings
to me

00:10:44.534 --> 00:10:47.701
and filled me up with da air!"

00:10:47.701 --> 00:10:49.701
[Normal voice]
So, the first hearing

00:10:49.701 --> 00:10:51.734
actually ended up
scoring big in the ratings,

00:10:51.734 --> 00:10:53.968
even though one channel
conspicuously decided

00:10:53.968 --> 00:10:55.868
not to air it,
which was, of course, Fox News.

00:10:55.868 --> 00:10:58.367
Fox News stuck with
its normal prime-time shows.

00:10:58.367 --> 00:11:01.167
Not just that, they also didn't
show commercials

00:11:01.167 --> 00:11:03.200
for the entire two hours
that the hearing was on,

00:11:03.200 --> 00:11:05.734
because they didn't want their
viewers to change the channel

00:11:05.734 --> 00:11:07.367
and see the hearing
on a different network.

00:11:07.367 --> 00:11:10.868
-They didn't take any commercial
breaks for the entire two hours

00:11:10.868 --> 00:11:12.567
when the hearing
was taking place.

00:11:12.567 --> 00:11:14.267
The reason you would not
take a commercial break

00:11:14.267 --> 00:11:16.734
is because you do not want
your viewers to have a chance

00:11:16.734 --> 00:11:19.267
to click over to another channel
to see what's going on.

00:11:19.267 --> 00:11:22.234
You want to keep them
with you the whole time.

00:11:22.234 --> 00:11:25.334
Last night, Fox News eliminated
two hours of commercial breaks,

00:11:25.334 --> 00:11:27.133
at the cost of
I don't know how much money,

00:11:27.133 --> 00:11:28.467
thousands of dollars,

00:11:28.467 --> 00:11:31.634
all to keep their viewers' eyes
away from the truth

00:11:31.634 --> 00:11:34.534
that was airing on every other
news network in the country.

00:11:34.534 --> 00:11:36.100
-Think about that.
They were so desperate

00:11:36.100 --> 00:11:37.834
to keep their viewers
from seeing the hearing

00:11:37.834 --> 00:11:40.400
that they cost themselves money
by not airing commercials.

00:11:40.400 --> 00:11:44.334
You know how many Acorn
Stairlifts they could have sold?

00:11:44.334 --> 00:11:45.968
Though I don't think
that was necessary.

00:11:45.968 --> 00:11:48.434
If you've ever been in a home
where they watch Fox News,

00:11:48.434 --> 00:11:50.100
you know they're not big
on flipping around.

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:52.767
I'm pretty sure they just buy
the TV, put it on Fox,

00:11:52.767 --> 00:11:54.467
and then bury the remote
in the backyard.

00:11:54.467 --> 00:11:56.400
But still,
just think about that.

00:11:56.400 --> 00:11:57.734
Fox went an entire two hours

00:11:57.734 --> 00:11:59.801
without airing
one of their usual commercials

00:11:59.801 --> 00:12:02.934
for some dumb scam product
aimed solely at old people

00:12:02.934 --> 00:12:05.133
like gold coins,
tactical sunglasses,

00:12:05.133 --> 00:12:07.300
commemorative plates with
Ronald Reagan's face on them,

00:12:07.300 --> 00:12:09.934
or a MAGA teddy bear
with Donald Trump's voice.

00:12:09.934 --> 00:12:12.033
"I love my MAGA teddy bear!

00:12:12.033 --> 00:12:15.534
You just push his belly and he
says the most adorable things."

00:12:15.534 --> 00:12:18.467
-Then they did dumps.
They call 'em dumps.

00:12:18.467 --> 00:12:20.300
Big, massive dumps.

00:12:20.300 --> 00:12:22.000
[ Laughter ]

00:12:25.601 --> 00:12:27.601
-It's also not surprising
that Fox would want

00:12:27.601 --> 00:12:29.234
to keep its audience
from watching the hearing

00:12:29.234 --> 00:12:31.167
because in addition
to providing damning evidence

00:12:31.167 --> 00:12:33.067
that Trump knew the election
had not been stolen

00:12:33.067 --> 00:12:35.234
and that he orchestrated
a criminal plot

00:12:35.234 --> 00:12:36.734
to overthrow the government,
the hearing was also

00:12:36.734 --> 00:12:38.133
deeply embarrassing
for the Trump family.

00:12:38.133 --> 00:12:39.968
For example,
the committee played video

00:12:39.968 --> 00:12:42.367
of Trump's daughter Ivanka
saying she accepted

00:12:42.367 --> 00:12:44.133
Attorney General
Bill Barr's assessment

00:12:44.133 --> 00:12:45.467
that there was
no widespread fraud

00:12:45.467 --> 00:12:47.033
and that the election
had not been stolen,

00:12:47.033 --> 00:12:50.167
meaning she disagreed with her
father's stolen election lies.

00:12:50.167 --> 00:12:52.534
-Many of President Trump's
White House staff

00:12:52.534 --> 00:12:55.567
also recognized that
the evidence did not support

00:12:55.567 --> 00:12:58.100
the claims
President Trump was making.

00:12:58.100 --> 00:13:00.167
This is the president's daughter

00:13:00.167 --> 00:13:02.501
commenting
on Bill Barr's statement

00:13:02.501 --> 00:13:05.300
that the department found
no fraud sufficient

00:13:05.300 --> 00:13:07.234
to overturn the election.

00:13:07.234 --> 00:13:09.534
-How did that affect your
perspective about the election

00:13:09.534 --> 00:13:12.200
when Attorney General Barr
made that statement?

00:13:12.200 --> 00:13:14.367
-It affected my perspective.

00:13:14.367 --> 00:13:17.934
I respect Attorney General Barr.

00:13:17.934 --> 00:13:20.434
So I...

00:13:20.434 --> 00:13:22.601
accepted what he was saying.

00:13:22.601 --> 00:13:24.868
-Oh, you did? That's weird.
I don't remember you mentioning

00:13:24.868 --> 00:13:26.501
any of that in the two months
after the election,

00:13:26.501 --> 00:13:27.834
when your father planned a coup

00:13:27.834 --> 00:13:29.701
and fomented a mob
of armed insurrectionists

00:13:29.701 --> 00:13:31.167
and werewolves
to ransack the Capitol

00:13:31.167 --> 00:13:34.534
like a Black Friday sale
at a Bass Pro Shop.

00:13:34.534 --> 00:13:37.033
Ivanka, just like Barr
and Stepien and all the rest,

00:13:37.033 --> 00:13:38.567
could have easily
spoken up at the time,

00:13:38.567 --> 00:13:40.501
but instead she just
quietly faded away,

00:13:40.501 --> 00:13:41.701
hoping no one would notice.

00:13:41.701 --> 00:13:44.434
She basically tried to do
the Homer Simpson GIF.

00:13:44.434 --> 00:13:46.767
[ Laughter ]

00:13:46.767 --> 00:13:49.267
Also, this is just a side note,

00:13:49.267 --> 00:13:52.234
but I do love how they always
use the [bleep] cameras

00:13:52.234 --> 00:13:54.234
for these depositions.
Ivanka Trump

00:13:54.234 --> 00:13:56.334
was the most glamorous member
of the Trump family,

00:13:56.334 --> 00:13:59.534
and now she looks like me
doing my show during lockdown.

00:13:59.534 --> 00:14:01.300
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:14:01.300 --> 00:14:02.801
Piece...

00:14:02.801 --> 00:14:05.868
Real quick piece of advice,
Vank --

00:14:05.868 --> 00:14:08.934
Don't read the YouTube comments.

00:14:08.934 --> 00:14:12.767
Because people will have notes.

00:14:12.767 --> 00:14:14.667
But the most predictable
part of Ivanka saying

00:14:14.667 --> 00:14:15.968
she agreed with Barr

00:14:15.968 --> 00:14:17.968
was that her own father
threw her under the bus

00:14:17.968 --> 00:14:20.200
by responding the next day
on his social media site,

00:14:20.200 --> 00:14:21.767
where he essentially said
she had no idea

00:14:21.767 --> 00:14:23.067
what she was talking about.

00:14:23.067 --> 00:14:25.434
-Trump is downplaying
his daughter's involvement,

00:14:25.434 --> 00:14:27.667
writing on his
Truth Social platform,

00:14:27.667 --> 00:14:29.100
"Ivanka Trump
was not involved

00:14:29.100 --> 00:14:31.767
in looking at
or studying election results.

00:14:31.767 --> 00:14:34.934
She had long since checked out
and was, in my opinion,

00:14:34.934 --> 00:14:37.234
only trying to be respectful
to Bill Barr

00:14:37.234 --> 00:14:39.334
and his position
as attorney general.

00:14:39.334 --> 00:14:40.634
He sucked."

00:14:40.634 --> 00:14:41.701
[ Laughter ]

00:14:41.701 --> 00:14:43.334
-Even with his family
turning on him

00:14:43.334 --> 00:14:45.834
and millions of people watching
nationally televised hearings

00:14:45.834 --> 00:14:47.467
describing his
mental fragility,

00:14:47.467 --> 00:14:50.300
Trump still has
a way with words.

00:14:50.300 --> 00:14:52.167
[As Trump] "Mr. Barr was
derelict in his duties."

00:14:52.167 --> 00:14:53.334
No, that's too wordy.

00:14:53.334 --> 00:14:54.534
Let me say, let me think,
let me think.

00:14:54.534 --> 00:14:56.200
"When the moment called
for courage,

00:14:56.200 --> 00:14:57.534
Mr. Barr failed to answer."

00:14:57.534 --> 00:14:58.701
No, that's not quite right.

00:14:58.701 --> 00:14:59.834
Oh, it's on the tip
of my tongue.

00:14:59.834 --> 00:15:01.734
"He sucked."
That's it!

00:15:01.734 --> 00:15:02.901
[ Laughter ]

00:15:02.901 --> 00:15:05.701
These hearings have
so far been powerful,

00:15:05.701 --> 00:15:08.300
effective, and well-produced.
They've painstakingly proven

00:15:08.300 --> 00:15:09.734
that Trump and the people
around him

00:15:09.734 --> 00:15:12.434
knew what they were saying
was a brazen and dangerous lie,

00:15:12.434 --> 00:15:15.067
and that the riot was not
just some impulsive incident.

00:15:15.067 --> 00:15:17.501
It was part of a detailed plan
orchestrated by Donald Trump

00:15:17.501 --> 00:15:19.467
to stage a coup
and overturn the election.

00:15:19.467 --> 00:15:21.367
Trump's team tried
to tell him the truth,

00:15:21.367 --> 00:15:22.701
but he refused
to accept it.

00:15:22.701 --> 00:15:24.834
Meanwhile, Rudy saw
a drop of Scotch

00:15:24.834 --> 00:15:26.100
left at the bottom
of the bottle

00:15:26.100 --> 00:15:27.434
and was so desperate
to get it out...

00:15:27.434 --> 00:15:28.934
-He sucked.

00:15:28.934 --> 00:15:31.667
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:15:31.667 --> 00:15:33.801
[ Audience cheering ]

00:15:33.801 --> 00:15:35.801
-I'll accept it.
I'll accept it.

00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:39.667
-This has been "A Closer Look."

